{# The selected zone: rename it, read it, delete it — the admin half of the split manager.

   RENAME is checked against the AREA, not the org: names are unique per area (uniq_zone_area_name),
   so two areas may each hold a "Crater" and only a local collision is an error.
   → POST /areas/{uuid}/zones/{zoneUuid}/rename

   DELETE removes the GROUPING and not one record. The consequence is spelled out in plain English
   beside the button that causes it, and it asks first through the platform's confirm-modal
   controller — never the browser's own dialog.
   → POST /areas/{uuid}/zones/{zoneUuid}/delete

   A reader sees the same facts and neither form: administering is Manager-and-up.

   WITH NOTHING SELECTED it says so and stops. The dashboard only ever draws this widget for an
   area that HAS zones (the surface is presence-driven), but the widget library renders every
   widget the surface ships whatever the area holds — so an unzoned area reaches this template
   with `selected` null, and a pane of blanks would be a worse answer than one honest sentence. #}
{% if selected is null %}
    <div class="c" data-w="detail">
        <span class="tab"><span class="idx">—</span>No zone selected<span class="src">· nothing to administer</span></span>
        <p class="zhint">{{ area.name }} has no zones, so there is none to read, rename or delete. Import a
            zoning scheme and this pane fills with whichever zone you pick — one at a time, which is what
            this direction is for.</p>
    </div>
{% else %}
<div class="c" data-w="detail">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">{{ selected.plate }}</span>{{ selected.name }}<span class="src">· {{ canManage ? 'editing' : 'selected' }}</span></span>

    {% if canManage %}
        <form method="post" class="renamer" data-zone-rename
              action="{{ path('app_area_zone_rename', {uuid: area.uuid, zoneUuid: selected.uuid}) }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('zone_manage') }}">
            <span class="sw" style="background:{{ selected.color }};width:16px;height:16px"></span>
            <input class="fld" type="text" name="name" value="{{ selected.name }}" required maxlength="128"
                   aria-label="Rename “{{ selected.name }}”">
            <button class="cta" type="submit">Save</button>
        </form>
        <p class="zhint">A zone's name is <b>unique within its area</b> — {{ area.name }} cannot hold two zones called
            “{{ selected.name }}”. Renaming re-groups every number; it moves no record.</p>
    {% else %}
        <div class="renamer">
            <span class="sw" style="background:{{ selected.color }};width:16px;height:16px"></span>
            <span style="font-weight:600">{{ selected.name }}</span>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="detail-k">
        <div><b>{{ selected.areaKm2|number_format(0) }}<em> km²</em></b><span>area</span></div>
        <div><b>{{ selected.sharePct|number_format(1) }}<em>%</em></b><span>of the AOI</span></div>
        <div><b>{{ selected.vertices }}</b><span>vertices</span></div>
        <div><b>{{ zones|length }}</b><span>zones in this area</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="rln"><span>Geometry</span><span class="mono d">MultiPolygon · {{ selected.vertices }} vertices · EPSG:4326</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span>Address</span><span class="mono d">{{ selected.uuid }}</span></div>
    {# The call every module makes to put a waypoint or an incident under a zone — named here so the
       feature's actual payoff is visible from the screen that manages it. #}
    <div class="rln"><span>Point lookup</span><span class="mono d">ZoneService::zoneOf({{ area.name|lower }}, lon, lat)</span></div>

    {% if canManage %}
        <div class="dangerbar">
            {{ ux_icon('lucide:trash-2') }}
            <span><b>Delete this zone.</b> Everything it groups — patrols, incidents, every record any module
                counted under “{{ selected.name }}” — <b>stay exactly where they are</b>. They simply stop being
                grouped under that name.</span>
            <form method="post" data-zone-delete
                  action="{{ path('app_area_zone_delete', {uuid: area.uuid, zoneUuid: selected.uuid}) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('zone_manage') }}">
                <button class="btn" type="submit"
                        {{ stimulus_controller('confirm-modal') }}
                        data-action="click->confirm-modal#ask"
                        data-confirm-modal-title-value="Delete “{{ selected.name }}”?"
                        data-confirm-modal-message-value="The zone is removed from {{ area.name }}. No record is deleted with it — the patrols, incidents and everything else it grouped stay exactly where they are, and simply stop being grouped under this name. This cannot be undone."
                        data-confirm-modal-confirm-label-value="Delete zone"
                        data-confirm-modal-danger-value="true">Delete</button>
            </form>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}
